WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
Under a heading like Configuration,

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.940
a reader learns only the topic,

3
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.933
but Configure the client with an API key says what they'll do.

4
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:15.473
So the rule for documentation headings is that a heading tells a scanning reader what its section contains.

5
00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.687
For a procedure,

6
00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:19.027
I'd name the task or its result,

7
00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:22.133
like Create the project and install the CLI.

8
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.733
But that doesn't mean a verb in every heading,

9
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:28.413
because a concept or reference section gets a descriptive noun phrase,

10
00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:30.467
like Webhook signature headers.

11
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.387
So before you publish,

12
00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:34.507
read the headings without the body copy,

13
00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:37.827
and check that each one says why its section exists.
